WEBVTT

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.280
Micchan!

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.570
Let's have lunch!

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:08.990
Okay.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.030
Your lunches always look so good, Micchan!

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.610
You have a good mom.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.820
No, I make my own lunch.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:22.900
And Anzu's, too.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:23.900
What?

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.030
Mom leaves for work early.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.950
Wow, Micchan, I'm impressed.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.150
Wait, is that a Scotch egg?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.030
And you actually made that before school?

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.700
Shut up.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.950
And it's good!

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:37.900
Don't eat it!

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:42.860
Not that I really care, but you and Ishino...

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.360
Oh, yeah! The pancake place
by the station is crazy good!

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.570
Wow. You know a lot about sweets for a guy.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.320
No, actually, I really don't care.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.780
Good, you're here. Takanashi!

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.280
We just got a call from the hospital. It's your mother.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:20.740
Crying in a place like this,

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:26.740
No one will notice me. I know that

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:30.450
As if nothing ever happened,

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:36.150
The world alone moves forward, erasing the past

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:41.030
Even though I decided to photograph you on that film

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.530
The bottomless sky keeps accumulating

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:47.570
We may forget, but it doesn't disappear

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.280
That pain, remember? What was it?

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.950
If we get lost in the changing scenery,

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.070
We could try remembering that song

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:05.610
Yes, if we're together, even the sad things

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:09.400
Should eventually become treasures

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:18.530
I want to show you that you blended into the background

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:23.950
But didn't fade away that day

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:33.450
Chuo General Hospital

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.450
Chuo General Hospital
Episode 20
Regarding When my Friend
and my Maybe Friend Became Official.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.200
Episode 20
Regarding When my Friend
and my Maybe Friend Became Official.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.240
She has a concussion.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.820
Phew!

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.700
Phew...

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.450
I'm so sorry, Anzu. Mitsuya.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.780
I was doing some work and I fell off the stepladder.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.950
We're just glad you're okay!

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.700
Give me a break.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.860
We can't lose you, too, Mom, or this family is doomed.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.740
You have a good head on your shoulders. You'll be fine.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.530
The insurance money will at least
get you through high school.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.900
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.030
I'll take care of Anzu and the house,
so you just take it easy.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.490
I'll bring you some necessities tomorrow.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:10.570
Thanks.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.820
Anzu, what do you want for dinner tonight?

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:25.070
Note: A brown seaweed usually cooked with rice and fish dishes.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:22.950
Hijiki!

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.200
H-hijiki?

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:24.990
Uh-huh!

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.950
Okay, got it. You go on home now.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.240
Ishino.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.530
Is something wrong?

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:41.030
Why? Do I look like something's wrong?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.320
Uh-huh.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:46.780
And... do you usually
do the grocery shopping for your family?

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.740
No, but Mom couldn't today.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.030
She's going to be in the hospital for about three days.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:55.150
Oh, it's just a mild concussion.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.530
So it's just you and Anzu for three days?

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:58.530
Will you be okay?

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.030
Yeah. It's only three days. We'll be fine.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.200
Is there anything I can do?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.900
Uh, oh yeah. We're not really that close.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.400
I guess I'm meddling again.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.570
Yeah.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:13.240
And I don't need your pity, thanks.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:18.530
If anyone needs pity, it's me!

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:22.360
Me, the girl who can't get you
to ever even give her the time of day!

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:26.950
You said you'd ask me on a date,
but that promise goes unfulfilled to this very day!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.700
I'm the one who needs pity!

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.030
Wait, I don't think that's what we were talking about.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:34.320
That is what I really despise about you, Takanashi!

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.320
The way you act all cool so that
no one can see when you're struggling!

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.280
The way you always keep everyone at arm's length!

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.780
I thought we were friends!

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.740
And I'm okay with just being friends!

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.110
So let me help sometimes!

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.450
Bring it on!

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.400
My, what's going on?

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.530
What's that?

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:53.530
Let's go.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.320
Here...

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.280
Huh?

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.240
What am I, your bag carrier?

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:04.450
Wait up!

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.860
This isn't what I meant, you know.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.030
But I'll do it.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:17.570
Ishino, do you know how to prepare hijiki?

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:19.070
Actually, I do.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.950
I make it all the time with my grandma.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:21.990
Good!

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.400
Then you can cook the hijiki.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.280
What?!

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.700
What else can I do?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.110
Let me think.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.900
We couldn't go on our trip...

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.320
Still, I do want to do something for her
after she finishes remedial classes.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.150
But what?

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.490
How do you know where I live?!

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.030
It's been a while.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.200
Ugly four-eyes.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.820
If I say, "Yeah, good to see you," can we be done here?

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:01.950
B-between the legs...?

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.650
I heard you're going on a trip with Iroha.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:09.740
The thought of an otaku like you
spending a night alone with Iroha...

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:13.280
I know for a fact that your head
will be full of all kinds of freaky ideas.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.030
You disgust me.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.530
Just try and go on this trip.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.900
I will squash you like a bug.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:21.860
No.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.700
We're going on this trip.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.400
This is unusual.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:27.990
You want to fight me?

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.280
You want to go on this trip that badly, do you?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.820
No, you're going to hit me anyway.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:36.610
I just don't want you breaking my glasses again.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:37.900
Go on, I'm ready.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:40.900
You little... You really are maddening.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:43.570
I'm just gonna say, don't underestimate a virgin.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:47.150
As a matter of fact, I think I would feel
too unworthy to try anything with her.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:48.900
How can I be so sure?

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.200
I have no way of knowing
what kind of a person you really are.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.490
Th-that's a good point.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:07:00.740
But if it would make you feel better to promise
that I won't do anything, then I'll promise you right now.

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.700
I won't do anything to her.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:08.320
The only thing I want
is to make her wish come true, that's all.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:14.240
Dammit! Seriously, why did she choose you?

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.860
You don't know the first thing about Iroha!

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.360
Yeah.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:21.650
But...

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:24.450
There's no time.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:26.900
We're running out.

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:30.950
And I know that.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:34.650
That's why I want to give her what she wants.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.900
I never...

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.150
wanted to say it out loud again.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:45.530
Well, we're not going on a trip this time anyway.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:46.990
She has remedial classes.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.650
Are you done?

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.450
You still... had to hit me?

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.700
You do anything to her, and I will kill you.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.570
That hurts...

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:16.030
TAKANASHI

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.450
Here, Anzu. If you would do the honors.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:27.610
Yummy!

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:28.990
Thank you very much!

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.360
Last of all, we just need to mix in the miso?

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.450
Yeah.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.990
I can do that.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.400
Yeah, hold on a sec. I'll go get it.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.450
Here.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.400
Thanks.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:53.110
The two of us are kind of like
an old married couple, aren't we?

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:55.990
I feel like I've heard that comment before.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.820
Oh, the terrible things you said to me
on that camping trip.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:04.320
I think you said I had no sex appeal
and that I seemed like a pain in the ass...

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.320
You haven't let that go, huh?

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.740
But that's still how I see you, just so you know.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.530
Ouch... You really are mean, Takanashi.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.450
But you know, I've been thinking.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:23.280
Even if we did start a romantic relationship, I don't feel
like that would really close the distance between us.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.360
So I'm happy just being your best friend.

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:29.490
What?

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:32.530
Best friend? And you get to decide that without my input?

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:33.950
Because you say so, it's true?

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.860
Well, the food's done, so I'll be going.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:38.990
What? Really?

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.110
You're not going to eat with us?

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:42.070
What?

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.740
Well, I hope I'm not intruding.

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:49.570
This feels a little weird, doesn't it?

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:50.360
No.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.570
You're a nice kid, Anzu.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:56.990
Well it's not every day my brother
brings a girl to the house.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:03.150
The thing is, he asked me to come over
because he doesn't actually see me as a girl.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:07.650
See? He served my rice in this gigantic bowl.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:10.110
Because I know how much you eat, Ishino.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:13.240
I want my rice in a big bowl!

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.070
Why are you letting her influence you?

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.110
Stop it.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:19.030
Because her hijiki is really good!

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:21.530
Wow, not many kids your age like it.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:25.320
Hey, I know. You should come over
during the long weekend.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:27.360
I want you to make us more hijiki!

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:31.700
You don't already have plans for your day off?

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:35.990
Actually, I wanted to go
to an amusement park with Kaoru, but-

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.700
There's no way I'm letting you do that!

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:41.530
I don't know why you think you can
get away with it, but since his formal visit,

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.950
you have been spending way too much time
with him, every single day!

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:45.990
You sound like a stubborn old man.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:49.780
What's wrong with them going
to an amusement park? It's cute!

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:54.490
Ishino... there you go, sticking your nose
into other people's business again.

00:10:54.490 --> 00:10:56.070
Oh, it's my business.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.650
I helped you look for her when she ran away.

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:00.240
It's definitely my business.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:04.700
Our family has its own way of doing things!
You stay out of it!

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.450
They're kids in love, and you can't
just step back and watch over them?

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:09.200
Petty! You are so petty!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.900
I am not petty!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.610
No, you're totally petty.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.280
I-I'm so sorry.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.360
This is all my fault.

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:20.150
You made her cry.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:22.150
Wait, this is all my fault?

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.280
And we were having such a good time.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.610
Make up and be friends!

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:32.950
It's okay.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.070
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:38.650
It's not a bad thing to fall in love with someone.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.610
And of course if you love someone,

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.240
you're going to want to see them.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:46.400
Your brother just worries a little too much, that's all.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.320
Really?

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:50.860
Really. You're a good kid, Anzu.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:53.450
Then you'll be friends again?

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:54.740
Totally!

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:56.950
See? Best buds!

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:57.780
Yeah!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.490
What a relief!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:03.740
Oh, and I already have plans for the long weekend.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:06.990
But I made lots of hijiki, so I'll just put it in the freezer.

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.950
Okay. Thank you.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:22.400
So the long weekend...
you're going somewhere with Sakurada?

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.740
Oh, so you already know.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:28.360
Yeah. He was pretty excited when he told me about it.

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:29.110
Really?

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:31.740
Sakurada seems like a good person.

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:36.570
I've never had a good person like me before,
so I was honestly a little freaked out.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:38.490
A date? You're going on a date?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.700
Hmm, I guess... I am?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:49.860
To be honest, if it doesn't work out with a nice guy
like him, I figure I'm doomed. So there's a little fear there.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.990
But anyway, I'm just going
to stop resisting and have fun.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:55.950
What if...

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:00.610
What if... I told you not to go?

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:03.150
How would you mean that?

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:05.200
In a "I want you to come make hijiki" sense?

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.950
More of a "I don't want anyone taking you away" sense?

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:13.280
You know how that sounds, Takanashi?

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:16.030
It sounds like a "little boy
doesn't want anyone taking his toy" sense.

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:18.950
No, I mean it in the "my pet is running away" sense.

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.780
You're making me mad, Takanashi!

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.740
Whatever.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.450
I'm telling you not to go.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:26.950
So don't go.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.030
I'm going home!

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.530
No, wait!

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:36.990
I'm sorry, Anzu. See you later.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.110
Big Brother! Why did you fight with her again?

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:42.570
Now she's leaving!

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:47.900
Big Brother!

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:56.610
Anzu, you can go to the amusement park.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:57.530
What?

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.530
Ishino!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.490
Come on, wait!

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:17.240
It's not fair. It's not fair!

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.530
You're just toying with me.

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:30.650
I refuse to become a member
of your sexy girl squad, for your information.

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:32.450
Don't worry.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:35.070
You're definitely not sexy enough for that.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.280
I'm going to tell you what I'm thinking right now.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:44.240
I get the feeling, Ishino,
that you will be an important part of my life.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:48.650
And if I let you get away from me now,
I think I'm going to regret it.

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.400
So will you be my girlfriend? Or not?

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:55.700
Ishino.

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:04.070
Of course I'll be your girlfriend!

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:16.150
Huh? What?!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.990
Huh? Why...?

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:38.400
Why did you act like you had to work up
so much courage just to kiss me, huh?

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:42.070
Because I felt like I was opening a door
to a frightening world.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.030
Hey, are you sure you really love me?

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:49.070
I love you, Ishino.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:54.610
We'll go with that.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:57.700
You're infuriating!

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:03.280
The next day

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.610
So is everything still going okay, Ito?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:08.240
Huh?

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:10.860
You know. Your plans to spend the weekend with Ayado.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:11.900
Oh, that.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:15.900
It turns out it's just going to be dinner
at her house with her family.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.610
That's actually a pretty big challenge, too, you know.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:20.030
What? It is?

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:22.740
Wow, you really are grown up, Ito.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:24.530
What about you?

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:27.490
She's going to come over to my house for dinner.

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:30.240
So you're doing the same thing.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.150
Having someone come over
is not the same as going to them.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:39.650
Long Weekend Day One

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.280
Triple combo!

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.530
Right back at you!

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:41.530
Full combo!

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:44.070
Here goes!

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:45.150
Take that!

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.900
Is this really going to be okay?

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:47.610
Donuts combo!

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:48.900
Not bad!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:53.360
I'm sorry. My parents had something come up.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:54.240
What?!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.450
After you brought a hostess gift and everything.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.570
Oh, that's fine. I'll come another time!

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:00.150
That's okay.

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:04.240
They said they want you to make yourself at home,
so you're welcome to stay.

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.360
There's more where that came from!

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.110
Take that!

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.450
Aqua Water!

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:10.280
I lost again.

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:12.490
You're really good, Ayado.
I win!

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:15.780
I've gotten 100% on this game.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.570
But that's not the issue!

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:18.400
Ayado?

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:21.740
How many times are you going
to make me play against you?!

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.860
We've been playing video games for four hours.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:27.610
I am utterly astounded at how wholesomely
we're spending this time!

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:29.280
I... I'm sorry.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.820
On second thought, I really can't.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:49.700
Your parents must really trust me
to let me visit when they're gone.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.200
And look how I repay them.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:54.610
I need to take proper care of you, Ayado.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:01.360
When you say take proper care of me,

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:06.740
if you mean you won't touch me,
then you're making me very sad.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.860
I want you to know me better!

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:14.990
I want to teach you so much more about me.

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:24.400
I always thought Ayado was this
mysterious person who could do anything.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.610
But in reality, she's just been trying so hard on her own.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:31.110
When people are nice to her, it makes her cry.

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:35.110
Maybe that's
how lonely
she's always been

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:33.700
Maybe that's how lonely she's always been.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.320
I love you, Ayado.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:50.900
I love you, too, Senpai.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.400
Gyoza wrappers are made out of wheat flour.

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:06.320
Starch is the main component in the flour,
and when you add water and heat it,

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:09.320
it starts to get sticky, and forms a kind of paste.

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:10.950
That's called gelatinization-

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:13.450
That's really good! It's different than our usual gyoza!

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:15.950
Maybe because you made them, Big Sister.

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:18.030
Or maybe because we made them together.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:20.400
I'm glad we decided on gyoza hotpot.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:21.860
I think I'm going to eat too much.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.780
Your bowl is overflowing, Mom.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:24.990
Oh, my.

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.820
Iroha, you can come over for dinner anytime.

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:29.150
We're happy to have you.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.610
Thank you very much.

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:33.240
It's fun making gyoza.

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:34.450
I think so, too!

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.360
What is this?!

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.070
That's the octopus gyoza. And that one's squid.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:40.570
What?!

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:53.820
That was so much fun.

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:57.490
Thanks for coming.

00:19:57.490 --> 00:19:58.360
No problem.

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:02.200
I love going to your house, Tsutsun.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:06.570
Your mom, and dad, and Kaoru are all so nice.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:08.610
It's a lot of fun being with them.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:11.320
I wish we could spend more time together.

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:13.030
Me, too.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.030
Together forever...

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.450
Together forever...

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:22.570
Well then.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.700
I'd better be getting home.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.610
I'll walk you to your house.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.530
No. I'll be okay.

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:30.820
Goodnight, Tsutsun.

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:33.240
Uh... yeah, goodnight.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:41.530
Chuo General Hospital

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.740
So things are going well with him?

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:44.950
Yes, sir.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:46.240
I see.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:49.450
But it has to stop.

00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:53.780
You know I already gave in and indulged you once.

00:20:54.740 --> 00:20:56.740
You have one more month.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:58.820
Yes, sir.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.280
I wish we could have stayed together forever,

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:11.320
Tsutsun.

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:20.860
The rhythm of the dry leaves, the season of endings,

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:24.950
You led me by the hand

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:36.360
The white breath is the fading future (future)

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:54.400
Whether again or for the first time, show me your childlike face

00:21:55.570 --> 00:22:00.820
Could you meet the person you wanted to meet?

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:06.070
Could you be the person you wanted to be?

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:16.740
By being yourself, you helped me to be myself

00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:22.110
This day, today, when all we do is breathe,

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:27.360
Is more wonderful than anything

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:32.700
I don't need anything. Now let's go

00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:40.820
There's nothing to worry about
